{
  "kept": [
    {
      "id": "train-00-plain",
      "source_id": "train-00",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice, a schoolteacher and a writer, began to get tired of sitting by her sister on the bank. She had no pictures or conversations in it, “and what is the use of a book,” she thought."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-01-plain",
      "source_id": "train-01",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "She thought the rabbit was just a pig and would be a good dog to catch the rabbit."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-01-qa",
      "source_id": "train-01",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Why did the rabbit want to make her do this?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-02-plain",
      "source_id": "train-02",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "They could have won an award, but Alice decided to leave. Alice was not surprised, since the Rabbit had actually spotted a rabbit with either a waistcoat-pocket or a watch in the field."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-02-qa",
      "source_id": "train-02",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Why did Alice think it was so far out of her way to hear the Rabbit say to itself, “Oh dear! Oh dear! I shall be late!”?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-03-plain",
      "source_id": "train-03",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice was eventually able to get out of the zoo, but when she was gone, she was going to be able to go on some kind of adventure."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-03-qa",
      "source_id": "train-03",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "What did Alice put on the bed that day?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-04-plain",
      "source_id": "train-04",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice dipped quickly to the rabbit hole, and dipped suddenly down to the deep well."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-04-qa",
      "source_id": "train-04",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Why was Alice so tired and dehydrated?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-05-plain",
      "source_id": "train-05",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "She saw the jars filled with books and boxes, and it was found to be filled with books. But it was a little dark, and she found it styrily dark. So she found it labelled “OrANGE MARMALADE” to save it."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-06-plain",
      "source_id": "train-06",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "If you are a woman who is not brave, you will think you will fall down stairs. You will think you will fall down stairs, but you will think you will fall down stairs and you will not think you will fall down stairs."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-06-qa",
      "source_id": "train-06",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "What does the boy believe Alice to have fallen off the top of the house?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-07-plain",
      "source_id": "train-07",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "No, the fall had not gone. What they were doing was a great way to show off her knowledge. (And what would be the best title to say?)"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-07-qa",
      "source_id": "train-07",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "What kind of distance did Alice expect to take her?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-08-plain",
      "source_id": "train-08",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "A woman who was worried she would have to ask her if she would fall right, but she wasn’t even aware of the threat. She started to make a point of asking her."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-08-qa",
      "source_id": "train-08",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "What did the writer have to ask the girl to do?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-09-plain",
      "source_id": "train-09",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice began talking again. “Dinah” was the cat. “I hope they’ll remember her saucer of milk at tea-time. Dinah my dear! I wish you were down here with me!” (Dinah was the cat). “I hope you were down here with me! There are no mice in the air, I’m afraid, but you might catch a bat, and that’s very like a mouse. But do"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-09-qa",
      "source_id": "train-09",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "What does the female see as a sign of a cat’s thinning ability?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-10-plain",
      "source_id": "train-10",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice was a bit sad, but Alice ran down the stairs, the White Rabbit was quiet. She was afraid the Rabbit would not come up, and she jumped on to her feet. Alice looked up, and was just in time to hear it say, \"Oh my ears and whiskers, how late it’s getting!\" She had no idea what it was, but the Rabbit quickly came down to see it, and Alice was on the roof."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-10-qa",
      "source_id": "train-10",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "What did the tyrant find in the dark hallway?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-11-plain",
      "source_id": "train-11",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "The door was locked. It was a door that would have remained locked. Alice went through the door and walked sadly down the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-11-qa",
      "source_id": "train-11",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "What kind of door was Alice not locking?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-12-plain",
      "source_id": "train-12",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice had a table made of glass and made of concrete, so she walked around the hall, looking for a little door that could open the door, but, alas! There was nothing on it except a tiny golden key. She approached the door and tried the little golden key, and the door would not open any of them. She then took a curtain and started looking at it, the door that had a window outside."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-12-qa",
      "source_id": "train-12",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Which of the following is not a door shaped like a curtain?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-13-plain",
      "source_id": "train-13",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice did not know how to close up a doorway."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-13-qa",
      "source_id": "train-13",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "What happened to Alice and her family?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-14-plain",
      "source_id": "train-14",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice was looking for a key for her son, and she went back to the table. Alice would have been a little more knowledgeable about the rules, but this time she found a bottle that looked like a paper label. Alice found a small bottle, “which certainly was not here before,” and a paper label. Alice's book of rules was not there, but a book of rules for shutting people up like telescopes."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-14-qa",
      "source_id": "train-14",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Who was Alice looking for at the table?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-15-plain",
      "source_id": "train-15",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice didn’t have much to drink but she didn’t want to, and she didn’t even want to be a poker player."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-15-qa",
      "source_id": "train-15",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Who was reading \"Another Wild Wild\"?"
    },
    {
      "id": "train-16-plain",
      "source_id": "train-16",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "Alice found the bottle interesting."
    },
    {
      "id": "train-16-qa",
      "source_id": "train-16",
      "split": "train",
      "text": "What did Alice like the moment she finished it off?"
    }
  ],
